        # Instead, a hash table approach with a bunch of bounds runs slower, but uses less space complexity.    The merging of intervals across gaps is the only weird part...    I think it's still better for space and time complexity, though.   One could also use a sorted set
        intervals_hash = {}
        # hash each bound +/-1 to the other "end of the interval".  i.e. after you see your first 2, {1:3, 3:1   }
